AUDIX MCP DUAL-USE SECURITY DISCLOSURE

This package connects compatible coding agents to Audix's smart-contract
security testing service. It can upload a user-selected Foundry project,
track security analysis, and retrieve generated fuzz-test harnesses.

Intended legitimate use

Audix MCP is intended for defensive security testing, secure software
development, vulnerability research, and authorized assessment of smart
contracts. Users must test only software they own or are explicitly
authorized to assess and must comply with applicable laws and agreements.

Potential for misuse

Security testing and fuzzing capabilities can be applied to software without
authorization. Such use is outside the intended purpose of this package.

Operational boundaries

The client requires an authenticated Audix account, limits archive uploads to
an authorized project root, excludes common credential paths, and retrieves
only artifacts identified by the Audix service for the selected scan.
